# 2. The Three Pillars of Data Engineering

A useful way to understand data engineering is through three major pillars.

## 2.1 Data Production

Data production is the stage where data is generated.

Examples:

- A customer places an order.
- A payment is processed.
- A user clicks a button on a website.
- An IoT sensor measures temperature.
- An API returns customer or product information.

The Data Engineer must understand where the data originates, its format, how frequently it changes, and how it can be accessed.

## 2.2 Data Transformation

Transformation prepares raw data for reliable use.

Typical operations include:

- Removing duplicates
- Handling missing values
- Standardizing date formats
- Converting data types
- Joining datasets
- Validating business rules
- Aggregating records
- Parsing JSON
- Standardizing identifiers
- Creating derived columns

Transformation can be performed using SQL, Python, Apache Spark, or other processing engines.

## 2.3 Data Serving

Serving makes processed data available to consumers.

Examples include:

- Power BI dashboards
- Data warehouse tables
- Data marts
- Analytical SQL views
- Machine learning datasets
- Data APIs
- Curated files

## 2.4 The Overall Flow

```text
Data Production
      |
      v
Data Ingestion
      |
      v
Data Storage
      |
      v
Data Transformation
      |
      v
Data Quality Validation
      |
      v
Curated Data Products
      |
      v
Analytics | BI | Data Science | Applications
```

