# 5. Database Normalization

Normalization reduces unnecessary data duplication and helps prevent data anomalies.

## 5.1 First Normal Form (1NF)

A table generally satisfies 1NF when each field contains an atomic value under the chosen model and repeating groups are avoided.

Avoid storing multiple independent values in one field when they should be represented as separate records.

## 5.2 Second Normal Form (2NF)

A table must satisfy 1NF, and every non-key attribute must depend on the whole candidate key rather than only part of a composite key.

## 5.3 Third Normal Form (3NF)

A table must satisfy 2NF and avoid inappropriate transitive dependencies of non-key attributes on a key.

## 5.4 Why Normalization Matters

Normalization helps:

- Reduce unwanted duplication
- Improve consistency
- Prevent update anomalies
- Make transactional relationships clearer

Analytical systems may intentionally denormalize some data to simplify reporting queries.

