# 14. Cloud Providers and Data Lake Storage

## 14.1 Major Cloud Providers

- Microsoft Azure
- Amazon Web Services (AWS)
- Google Cloud Platform (GCP)

They offer similar categories of services, but their features, limitations, pricing, and integrations differ.

## 14.2 Object Storage

Object storage is used to store files and data objects at scale.

Common uses:

- Data lakes
- Application logs
- Backups
- Large datasets
- Analytics files
- Media objects

Object storage is not identical to a traditional file system, even when directory-like interfaces are provided.

## 14.3 Storage Service Examples

| Provider | Example Service |
|---|---|
| Azure | Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 |
| AWS | Amazon S3 |
| GCP | Google Cloud Storage |

## 14.4 Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2

ADLS Gen2 is an Azure data-lake storage offering built on Azure Blob Storage capabilities and supports a hierarchical namespace.

It can store:

- CSV
- JSON
- Parquet
- Logs
- Images
- Other structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data

Important considerations include:

- File sizes
- Partitioning
- Directory structure
- Access control
- Retention
- Data format
- Encryption
- Network access
- Lifecycle management

