### Apache Spark Concepts

**Distributed processing:** Work is divided across tasks and compute resources.

**Partitioning:** Data is divided into pieces for parallel processing.

**Shuffle:** Data is redistributed between partitions, often during joins and aggregations. Shuffles can be expensive.

**Caching:** Reusing data already materialized in memory or another supported storage layer can improve performance when appropriate.

Managed platforms reduce some infrastructure administration, but engineers still need to design efficient jobs and manage compute and cost.

